6. Hover the mouse over a plane — the hovered plane's material should show flag-wave vertex deformation (subtle Y-axis wave).
7. Resize the browser window — canvas should refit correctly via `ResizeObserver`, aspect ratio should stay correct.
8. Scroll the page so the gallery section is out of viewport — RAF should pause (IntersectionObserver). Return to viewport — RAF should resume. Confirm via DevTools Performance tab that no `requestAnimationFrame` callbacks fire when hidden.
9. Navigate away from the page and back — `dispose()` should fire cleanly with no WebGL context leak. Confirm in DevTools → Application → WebGL that no orphaned contexts accumulate.
10. Check browser console for zero errors. Specifically: no "Unable to use a texture from a deallocated context" WebGL errors, no "Cannot read properties of null" from the RAF firing after dispose.

